    "created_at": "2020-01-25T18:51:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-25T18:51:49Z",
    "body": "> I think we should fire it in each browsing context when that context next becomes visible.\r\n\r\nThis may be unnecessary, but I wonder about a potential optimization to this: fire for all windows where the top-level browsing context is same-origin with the one which just became visible (and received the event).\r\n\r\nThe reason for this is that if any window in your origin gets the event, it can already message it to all other same-origin windows (e.g. by setting `localStorage` or using `BroadcastChannel`.)  It would address the frequent use case of simultaneously reloading all windows that wait for the `onLine` event, without requiring scripting.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
